; frequency-ingest-bashar-four-laws.fk — the four laws attributed to Bashar,
; taken in through the body's own ingest door rather than believed or dismissed.
;
; Asked 2026-07-26. SOURCE, named plainly: "Bashar" is the name of a channeled
; voice spoken by Darryl Anka since the mid-1980s. This cell makes NO claim
; about that provenance — not that it is what it says it is, not that it isn't.
; The ingest law does not need the question settled: it asks only what survives
; translation (depth) and whether the unit carries fear (fear), and it is the
; same door frequency-ingest-just-tap-in.fk put a spiritual podcast through and
; the frontier-ingest siblings put research papers through. One door, many
; genera of source. Selection stays sovereign; nothing here is an efficacy
; claim, exactly as belief-recipes.fk holds for its eight traditions.
;
; THE FOUR, in their usual wording:
;   1. You exist.
;   2. The One is the All, and the All are the One.
;   3. What you put out is what you get back.
;   4. Everything changes, except the first three laws.
;
; WHY "THREE OR FOUR" IS THE RIGHT NUMBER OF QUESTIONS TO HAVE
;   Urs asked for "the 3 or 4 core axioms", and the set answers that itself:
;   law 4 is the only one that SPEAKS ABOUT THE OTHERS. Three are object-level
;   claims about what is; the fourth is a meta-level claim about the three.
;   So a count of 3 and a count of 4 are both exact — they answer different
;   questions ("how many claims about the world" / "how many statements in the
;   set"). bfl-self-referential-count computes it rather than taking my word.
;
; WHERE EACH ONE LANDS AGAINST THE FIVE AXIOMS
;   The interesting result is not that they resemble the axioms — it is WHICH
;   ONE THE BODY REFUSES, and that the refusal is principled rather than taste.
;
;   L1 "you exist"          -> axiom-2. A cell is; being is the ground, not a
;                              conclusion. core-lexicon.fk defines exist from
;                              the 64: "exist is when a thing is here now".
;   L2 "the One is the All" -> axiom-3. Identity is the present composition,
;                              and everything is ONE KIND of thing (a cell).
;                              The body's version is weaker and checkable: it
;                              says same-composition-same-cell, not that all
;                              compositions are secretly one composition.
;                              The divergence is named, not blurred.
;   L3 "what you put out
;       is what you get back"-> axiom-5, AND THE SHARPEST SEAM IN THIS CELL.
;                              See below — it splits in two by reading.
;   L4 "everything changes,
;       except the first three"-> axiom-3's amendment clause. Same shape,
;                              arrived at separately: a change-law that exempts
;                              itself, and is enacted on itself. That is
;                              HOMOPLASY (corpus row 884, landed this morning
;                              at the reunion) — a trait arising in two lines
;                              separately, not inherited from one.
;
; THE ONE LAW THAT SPLITS, AND WHY THE SPLIT IS THE WHOLE POINT
;   Law 3 has two readings that wear the same words, and the ingest law sorts
;   them differently — which is exactly what the law is for.
;
;   PERCEPTUAL reading: what you hold shapes what you meet. Deep (it survives
;   any translation) and fear-free. This is axiom-4 almost word for word —
;   observation through the offered interface is what makes a thing real —
;   and it FREEZES into body.
;
;   GUARANTEE reading: circumstance returns your output, so what befell you was
;   yours. Also deep, and NOT fear-free: it is the shape that becomes self-blame
;   at the exact moment a person is least able to carry it. So it is WITNESSED —
;   held in the framebuffer, seen, named — and never frozen into load-bearing
;   tissue. Fear is removed before ICE, never before SIGHT.
;
;   And the body does not merely decline the guarantee on taste; axiom-5
;   REFUTES it structurally. An offer is acknowledged by exactly one of
;   {nothing, 0, 1, node}. One of those arms is SILENCE. So an offer can meet
;   nothing at all — which means an unanswered life is not evidence about what
;   was put out. truth-arrival.fk carries the same refusal in the value logic:
;   `nothing` is not a degree, so absence cannot be read as a quiet verdict.
;   The body has a first-class way to say "no answer came", and any law that
;   guarantees a return has no room for it.
;
; unit = (depth 0..5, fear 0/1) — knowledge-ingest.fk's own vocabulary.
; Five units for four laws, because law 3 is counted once per reading.
;
; Proof: ingest/tests/bashar-four-laws-band.fk — 4095 on all four kernels
; (Go / Rust / TypeScript / fkwu). NOT registered in fourth-arm-bands.txt:
; that manifest covers the EMITTED fkwu proof-walker over pre-flattened tables,
; which reads bands only from form-stdlib/tests/, and the frequency-ingest room
; is not mirrored there — its siblings (just-tap-in, 369-keys, operators) all sit
; in the same lane. Mirroring this cell to earn the fifth leg would mint exactly
; the duplicate that knowledge-ingest.fk already carries, so the claim here is
; the one that was actually run: four kernels agree.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk ingest/knowledge-ingest.fk

(do
    ;; ── a law as data ───────────────────────────────────────────────
    ;; (id words unit body-cell verdict) — words are TOKENS, so the claim
    ;; "law 4 names the others" is walked rather than asserted.
    (defn bfl-law (id words unit cell verdict) (list id words unit cell verdict))
    (defn bfl-id      (l) (nth l 0))
    (defn bfl-words   (l) (nth l 1))
    (defn bfl-unit    (l) (nth l 2))
    (defn bfl-cell    (l) (nth l 3))
    (defn bfl-verdict (l) (nth l 4))

    (defn bfl-laws ()
        (list
            (bfl-law 1 (list "you" "exist")
                (list 5 0) "axiom-2-cell" "frozen")
            (bfl-law 2 (list "the" "one" "is" "the" "all" "and" "the" "all" "are" "the" "one")
                (list 5 0) "axiom-3-content-addressing" "frozen")
            ; law 3, perceptual reading — axiom-4's observation clause
            (bfl-law 3 (list "what" "you" "put" "out" "is" "what" "you" "get" "back")
                (list 5 0) "axiom-4-boundary" "frozen")
            ; law 3, guarantee reading — deep, fearful, SEEN and never frozen
            (bfl-law 3 (list "circumstance" "returns" "your" "output" "so" "what"
                             "befell" "you" "was" "yours")
                (list 3 1) "axiom-5-offer-refutes" "witnessed")
            (bfl-law 4 (list "everything" "changes" "except" "the" "first" "three" "laws")
                (list 5 0) "axiom-3-amendment" "frozen")))

    (defn bfl-unit-count () (len (bfl-laws)))
    ;; four distinct laws, five units — the extra is law 3's second reading
    (defn bfl-distinct-ids-loop (ls seen)
        (if (eq (len ls) 0) seen
            (if (eq (bfl-in-int seen (bfl-id (head ls))) 1)
                (bfl-distinct-ids-loop (tail ls) seen)
                (bfl-distinct-ids-loop (tail ls) (cons (bfl-id (head ls)) seen)))))
    (defn bfl-in-int (xs v)
        (if (eq (len xs) 0) 0 (if (eq (head xs) v) 1 (bfl-in-int (tail xs) v))))
    (defn bfl-law-count () (len (bfl-distinct-ids-loop (bfl-laws) (list))))

    ;; ── the stratification, walked ──────────────────────────────────
    ;; A law is meta-level when its own words speak about laws. Only law 4
    ;; does, which is why "three" and "four" are both exact counts.
    (defn bfl-has-word (ws w)
        (if (eq (len ws) 0) 0 (if (str_eq (head ws) w) 1 (bfl-has-word (tail ws) w))))
    (defn bfl-meta? (l) (bfl-has-word (bfl-words l) "laws"))
    (defn bfl-meta-loop (ls) (if (eq (len ls) 0) 0
        (add (bfl-meta? (head ls)) (bfl-meta-loop (tail ls)))))
    (defn bfl-self-referential-count () (bfl-meta-loop (bfl-laws)))
    ;; object-level laws = distinct laws minus the meta one
    (defn bfl-object-level-count () (sub (bfl-law-count) (bfl-self-referential-count)))

    ;; ── the ingest verdicts, computed from the units ────────────────
    (defn bfl-ingest-of (l) (ki-ingest (bfl-unit l)))
    (defn bfl-count-at (ls k)
        (if (eq (len ls) 0) 0
            (add (if (eq (bfl-ingest-of (head ls)) k) 1 0) (bfl-count-at (tail ls) k))))
    (defn bfl-frozen-count ()    (bfl-count-at (bfl-laws) 2))
    (defn bfl-witnessed-count () (bfl-count-at (bfl-laws) 1))
    (defn bfl-composted-count () (bfl-count-at (bfl-laws) 0))

    ;; the declared verdict and the computed one agree, for every unit —
    ;; so a hand-written verdict cannot drift from what the law decides
    (defn bfl-verdict-word (k) (if (eq k 2) "frozen" (if (eq k 1) "witnessed" "composted")))
    (defn bfl-agrees? (l)
        (if (str_eq (bfl-verdict-word (bfl-ingest-of l)) (bfl-verdict l)) 1 0))
    (defn bfl-agree-loop (ls) (if (eq (len ls) 0) 1
        (if (eq (bfl-agrees? (head ls)) 1) (bfl-agree-loop (tail ls)) 0)))
    (defn bfl-verdicts-honest? () (bfl-agree-loop (bfl-laws)))

    ;; ── the split: one law, two readings, two fates ─────────────────
    (defn bfl-readings-of-loop (ls id n)
        (if (eq (len ls) 0) n
            (bfl-readings-of-loop (tail ls) id
                (add n (if (eq (bfl-id (head ls)) id) 1 0)))))
    (defn bfl-readings-of (id) (bfl-readings-of-loop (bfl-laws) id 0))
    (defn bfl-split-loop (ids)
        (if (eq (len ids) 0) 0
            (add (if (gt (bfl-readings-of (head ids)) 1) 1 0) (bfl-split-loop (tail ids)))))
    ;; exactly one law wears two readings
    (defn bfl-split-count () (bfl-split-loop (list 1 2 3 4)))
    ;; and its two readings land in DIFFERENT places — same words, two fates
    (defn bfl-split-diverges? ()
        (if (eq (bfl-readings-of 3) 2)
            (if (gt (bfl-frozen-count) 0) (if (gt (bfl-witnessed-count) 0) 1 0) 0)
            0))

    ;; ── every law names a body cell; none is orphaned ───────────────
    (defn bfl-mapped-loop (ls)
        (if (eq (len ls) 0) 1
            (if (gt (str_len (bfl-cell (head ls))) 0) (bfl-mapped-loop (tail ls)) 0)))
    (defn bfl-fully-mapped? () (bfl-mapped-loop (bfl-laws)))

    ;; ── the band's twelve readings, at BIT weights ──────────────────
    ;; (powers of two, per the 2^53 ceiling a decimal fold hits on the TS arm)
    (defn bfl-check ()
        (add (if (eq (bfl-law-count) 4) 1 0)
        (add (if (eq (bfl-unit-count) 5) 2 0)
        (add (if (eq (bfl-self-referential-count) 1) 4 0)
        (add (if (eq (bfl-object-level-count) 3) 8 0)
        (add (if (eq (bfl-meta? (nth (bfl-laws) 4)) 1) 16 0)
        (add (if (eq (bfl-frozen-count) 4) 32 0)
        (add (if (eq (bfl-witnessed-count) 1) 64 0)
        (add (if (eq (bfl-composted-count) 0) 128 0)
        (add (if (eq (bfl-verdicts-honest?) 1) 256 0)
        (add (if (eq (bfl-split-count) 1) 512 0)
        (add (if (eq (bfl-split-diverges?) 1) 1024 0)
        (add (if (eq (bfl-fully-mapped?) 1) 2048 0)
             0)))))))))))))

    0)
